    <!-- §1 Overview -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="overview">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§1</div>
        <h2>System Overview</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        The Trade Claim module is the entry point for institutional cross-border liquidity requests.
        A commercial bank operator originates a claim against an active FX corridor, names the
        beneficiary institution in the destination country, specifies the liquidity amount, and submits
        the claim into a multi-tier supervisory review queue. Every field transition, submission, and
        status change is captured in an immutable audit chain.
      </p>

      <div class="dp-pane-grid">
        <div class="dp-pane dp-pane-left">
          <h3>Left Pane — Claiming Institution</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Country selector (54 AU members)</li>
            <li>Central Bank SWIFT code (auto-populated)</li>
            <li>Central Bank name (read-only)</li>
            <li>Central Bank Holder ID (hidden field)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="dp-pane dp-pane-middle">
          <h3>Middle Pane — Trade Details</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Trade Corridor (scrollable list)</li>
            <li>Destination institution (corridor-filtered)</li>
            <li>SWIFT code &amp; role (auto-populated)</li>
            <li>Commercial Bank Holder ID (DB-resolved)</li>
            <li>Trade direction, amount, currency</li>
            <li>Beneficiary name &amp; country</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="dp-pane dp-pane-right">
          <h3>Right Pane — Claim Metadata</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Invoice reference</li>
            <li>Trade description</li>
            <li>Submitted-by operator identity</li>
            <li>Submit / Save Draft actions</li>
            <li>Compliance declaration</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>Operational Context</h3>
      <p>
        Trade claims are not free-form requests. Every claim must reference an active, unfrozen FX
        corridor and a registered commercial bank in the destination country. The system resolves the
        Commercial Bank Holder ID from the <code>commercial_bank_holder_keys</code> table using the
        institution's SWIFT code before submission is permitted. Claims that cannot resolve a holder ID
        require manual operator intervention at the Qt6 desktop client.
      </p>
      <div class="dp-callout dp-info">
        <span class="dp-ci">ℹ</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Sovereign settlement scope:</strong> Trade claims feed directly into the corridor
          liquidity reserve system. An approved claim authorises the drawdown of corridor reserve
          funds and triggers the issuance eligibility gates at the Supervisor Desk. No CBDC is issued
          until all five gates pass.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="dp-callout dp-info">
        <span class="dp-ci">ℹ</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Who may create a claim — the dealer-bank maker.</strong> The
          <code>commercial_institution_operator</code> role (Commercial Institution Operator / Authorized
          Dealer — Claim Maker) is the only non-sovereign role. It holds exactly two scopes —
          <code>claim.create</code> and <code>claim.read</code> — and is the intended claim originator.
          It is <strong>enclosed to its own institution</strong>: the trade-claim list is filtered by
          <code>submitted_by_institution_swift</code>, so a maker sees only claims their own institution
          submitted — never other counterparties' or central-bank claims. It has <strong>zero sovereign
          access</strong> (Issuance, Supervisor Desk, Deposit &amp; Burn, Corridor Ops, Validation,
          Governance are all hard-blocked). Four-eyes still applies downstream: the minter must differ
          from <code>submitted_by_operator_id</code>.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- §2 Workflow States -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="workflow">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§2</div>
        <h2>Workflow State Machine</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>State</th><th>Display Label</th><th>Entry Condition</th><th>Allowed Transitions</th><th>Actor</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="s-pending">draft</span></td>
            <td>Draft</td>
            <td>Operator saves without submitting</td>
            <td>→ pending_review, → cancelled</td>
            <td>Originating operator</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="s-pending">pending_review</span></td>
            <td>Pending Review</td>
            <td>Operator submits completed form</td>
            <td>→ approved, → rejected, → clarification_requested, → cancelled</td>
            <td>Supervisor</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="s-active">approved</span></td>
            <td>Approved</td>
            <td>Supervisor approves; all five gates pass</td>
            <td>Terminal (settlement proceeds)</td>
            <td>Supervisor</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="s-expired">rejected</span></td>
            <td>Rejected</td>
            <td>Supervisor rejects with mandatory notes</td>
            <td>Terminal</td>
            <td>Supervisor</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="s-pending">clarification_requested</span></td>
            <td>Clarification Requested</td>
            <td>Supervisor flags missing or inconsistent data</td>
            <td>→ pending_review (on resubmission)</td>
            <td>Supervisor → Originating operator</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="s-expired">cancelled</span></td>
            <td>Cancelled</td>
            <td>Operator or supervisor cancels before approval</td>
            <td>Terminal</td>
            <td>Originating operator or Supervisor</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h3>State Transition Diagram</h3>
      <div class="dp-flow">
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Draft (optional)</h4><p>Operator saves incomplete claim. <code>POST /api/v2/trade_claims/draft</code>. Returns DRAFT-{timestamp} reference. Not visible in supervisor queue.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Submit → pending_review</h4><p>Operator submits complete claim. <code>POST /api/v2/trade_claims</code>. Status set to <code>pending_review</code>. Claim enters supervisor queue immediately.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Supervisor review</h4><p>Supervisor opens claim in Supervisor Desk. Five-gate eligibility evaluation runs. Supervisor selects Approve, Reject, Request Clarification, or Cancel.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Approved</h4><p><code>POST /api/v2/trade_claims/:id/approve</code>. Status → <code>approved</code>. <code>eligibility.issuance_eligible = true</code>. All five gates return <code>passed: true</code>.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Governor review (high-value)</h4><p>Claims above corridor daily cap threshold are escalated to Governor Desk before final settlement. Governor review is separate from supervisor approval.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Settlement</h4><p>Approved claims trigger corridor liquidity drawdown. CBDC issuance authorisation created against corridor reserve pool.</p></div>
      </div>

      <h3>Timeout &amp; Retry Behaviour</h3>
      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Scenario</th><th>Behaviour</th><th>Recovery</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Submission network failure</td><td>Client shows inline error. No state change on server.</td><td>Operator retries. Idempotency: duplicate reference within 60s returns the existing record.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Draft auto-expiry</td><td>Draft claims not submitted within 72h are auto-archived.</td><td>Operator must create new claim.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Clarification timeout</td><td>Claims in <code>clarification_requested</code> for &gt;7 days trigger supervisor alert.</td><td>Supervisor may cancel or re-route.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Supervisor inactivity</td><td>Claims in <code>pending_review</code> for &gt;24h escalate to supervisor manager queue.</td><td>Escalation notification dispatched.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
    </div>

    <!-- §3 Data Model -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="data-model">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§3</div>
        <h2>Data Model</h2>
