      <h3>Submit Payload</h3>
      <div class="dp-rule">POST /api/v2/trade_claims</div>
      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Source</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="f">corridor_id</td><td>tc_corridor_id</td><td>Resolved to corridor snapshot server-side</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="f">institution_id</td><td>tc_institution_id</td><td>Resolved to institution snapshot server-side</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="f">source_country</td><td>SC_PORTAL.country_code</td><td><strong>Explicit origin</strong> — the claiming institution's home ISO. Prevents corridor collapse (see callout).</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="f">target_country</td><td>tc_beneficiary_country</td><td><strong>Explicit destination</strong> — the beneficiary ISO. Server prefers this explicit pair over inference.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="f">origin_country_code / destination_country_code</td><td>same pair (aliases)</td><td>Sent for downstream corridor routing / display.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="f">amount</td><td>tc_amount</td><td>Numeric string</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="f">currency_code</td><td>tc_currency_code (hidden)</td><td>Derived from corridor</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="f">trade_direction</td><td>tc_trade_direction</td><td>import | export | remittance | interbank</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="f">beneficiary_name</td><td>tc_beneficiary_name</td><td></td></tr>
          <tr><td class="f">beneficiary_country</td><td>tc_beneficiary_country</td><td>ISO 3166-1 alpha-3</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="f">reference</td><td>tc_reference (optional)</td><td>Falls back to TC-{timestamp}</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="f">description</td><td>tc_description</td><td></td></tr>
          <tr><td class="f">submitted_by</td><td>tc_submitted_by</td><td>Falls back to institution name</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h3>Success Response (HTTP 201)</h3>
      <div class="dp-rule">{"status":"submitted","data":{...claim record...},"message":"Trade claim TC-... submitted — entering supervisory review queue."}</div>

      <div class="dp-callout dp-warn"><span class="dp-ci">⚠</span><div>
        <strong>Explicit corridor routing (no self-referential collapse).</strong> The client now sends
        the origin/destination pair explicitly (<code>source_country</code> from
        <code>SC_PORTAL.country_code</code>, <code>target_country</code> from the beneficiary), and the
        server <code>resolve_corridor!</code> prefers that explicit pair. This fixes the earlier defect
        where a claim with no source resolved to a same-country corridor (e.g. <code>NGA → NGA</code>) —
        a GHA→NGA claim now routes correctly.
      </div></div>
      <div class="dp-callout dp-info"><span class="dp-ci">ℹ</span><div>
        <strong>Client conveniences.</strong> Step&nbsp;2 shows a <strong>dynamic FX oracle label</strong>
        chosen by the destination central bank (national CB, else the regional oracle), and the destination
        <strong>holder ID auto-provisions</strong> from the target node (e.g. <code>BAPANANX-NAM-NODE-01</code>).
        These are display/routing aids; corridor rate, liquidity, and backing remain server-authoritative.
      </div></div>
    </div>

